.page rmdir 1 remove empty directories

# SYNOPSIS
*rmdir* _DIRECTORY_...

# DESCRIPTION
`rmdir` removes each _DIRECTORY_, which must be empty. To remove a directory with its contents use `rm -r`; to keep a copy in the Netherworld use trash(1).

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if any directory could not be removed.

# SEE ALSO
mkdir(1), rm(1), trash(1)
